# REGRESSION -- an indirect call whose callee is a NON-IDENTIFIER expression
# (`arr[0]`) on a `Callable[void(int &)]` element writes through to the
# caller's `int` slot exactly as calling `bump(&a)` directly does.
#
# AXIS / CELL (Track K, non-identifier callee axis):
#   Vector-of-Callable storage x plain-local int root x `&`-arg spelling.
# Sibling of `callable_amp_fntype_writethrough.gg` (identifier callee, LOCAL)
# and `sound_callable_amp_param_projection.gg` (identifier callee, PARAM); the
# discriminator here is the callee SHAPE (Vector index vs. bare name), not
# the arg's root.
#
# Pre-Track-K (measured at gorget-1 tip `1ec3ba55`): `gg check` clean, `gg
# build` clean, binary exits 139 (SIGSEGV) on BOTH C and LLVM. Root cause is
# TWO-LAYER:
#   1. `GirType::FnPtr` at `src/ir/types.rs` had no `param_ownerships` axis,
#      so the `Type::Function` mapper at `src/ir/lowering/types.rs` dropped
#      the `&` sigil at the AST->GIR boundary.
#   2. `infer_collection_element_type` at `src/ir/lowering/exprs/methods.rs`
#      built an EMPTY-params FnPtr for `Vector[Callable[...]]` elements --
#      sized right for the 16-byte GorgetClosure (attack_82 fix) but with
#      the signature lost -- so even after fixing step 1 the read side at
#      the non-identifier arm at `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs` had
#      nothing to consult.
#
# Fix (Track K): (a) extend `GirType::FnPtr` with `param_ownerships`; (b) add
# `TypeMapper::callable_alias_sigs` populated at `register_callable_inner_if_any`
# where the `Type::Function` inner is still in scope; (c) teach
# `infer_collection_element_type` to look up the sig; (d) route the
# non-identifier arm's args through `lower_call_arg` on the recovered sig
# (mirroring B1's identifier-callee fix).
#
# INTENDED (asserted): 101. Same reference-grade semantics as the
# `callable_amp_fntype_writethrough.gg` LOCAL-callee sibling.
void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void main():
    int a = 1
    Vector[Callable[void(int &)]] arr = []
    arr.push(bump)
    arr[0](&a)
    print(a)
